  "issue_number": 3464,
  "issue_title": "Add an axon-removals \"churn\" panel next to the network operations leaderboard",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\nThe current issue body says: \"GET /api/v1/chain/axon-removals \u2014 the teardown-side complement of the serving leaderboard above, unconsumed.\" That route is live and computes network-wide axon-teardown activity (`AxonInfoRemoved` events) over a 7d/30d window (`src/chain-axon-removals.mjs`, `ChainAxonRemovalsArtifact` in `src/contracts.mjs:1311-1314`), but it has **zero frontend touchpoint**: no query function calls it in `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts`, and no `ChainAxonRemovals` type exists in `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts`. The only axon-removals code in the frontend today is the *subnet-scoped* sibling (`subnetAxonRemovalsQuery` / `SubnetAxonRemovals`, queries.ts:3006-3018), which is itself unwired into any component and out of scope here.\n\n## Requirement\n\nRender a network-wide \"churn\" panel on the `/explorer` route showing axon-teardown activity (distinct removers, total removals, removals-per-remover, and a per-subnet leaderboard) for the same 7d/30d window already used by the rest of the explorer dashboard, placed next to (or directly below) the network operations leaderboard from #3463.\n\n## Backend\n\n- Endpoint: `GET /api/v1/chain/axon-removals` \u2014 accepts `?window=7d|30d` and `?limit=` (leaderboard cap, default 20 max 100); also supports `?format=csv` for the per-subnet leaderboard (`src/contracts.mjs:3031-3035`).\n- Response shape (confirmed from `buildChainAxonRemovals` in `src/chain-axon-removals.mjs:127-196`): `{ schema_version, window, observed_at, subnet_count, network: { distinct_removers, removals, removals_per_remover }, intensity_distribution: { count, mean, min, p25, median, p75, p90, max } | null, subnets: [{ netuid, distinct_removers, removals, removals_per_remover }] }` (subnets pre-sorted by `removals` desc).\n- Query function: **none exists.** No `chainAxonRemovalsQuery` (or equivalent) is defined anywhere in `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts`, and no corresponding type exists in `types.ts`. This PR must add both the typed query function AND the UI wiring in one PR \u2014 a data-layer-only PR is exactly the failure mode this rewrite exists to prevent. Model the new query on the existing `chainFeesQuery` (queries.ts:2371-2397), which is the closest sibling: same `ChainWindow` param type (queries.ts:2177), same `apiFetch` + `isRecord`/`firstString`/`firstFiniteNumber` normalization idiom, same `staleTime: STALE_SHORT`. Add a `ChainAxonRemovals` interface to `types.ts` mirroring the existing `SubnetAxonRemovals` interface (types.ts:1167-1175) but with the network/leaderboard shape above instead of the flat per-subnet fields.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- File(s) to change: `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` (add `chainAxonRemovalsQuery` + a `normalizeChainAxonRemovals`-style helper), `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` (add `ChainAxonRemovals`), and `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx` (520 lines \u2014 confirmed current) for the UI wiring.\n- Exact anchor: `ExplorerDashboard()` in `explorer.tsx` (function starts at line 225) already fetches four chain-wide queries via `useSuspenseQuery` at lines 230-233 (`chainActivityQuery`, `chainFeesQuery`, `chainCallsQuery`, `chainSignersQuery`) using the shared `win` window state from `search.window` (line 228). Add `chainAxonRemovalsQuery(win)` as a fifth `useSuspenseQuery` call there, and add its path to the `ApiSourceFooter` `paths` array (line 78-83).\n- What to render: a new `<section className=\"rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-5\">` block, matching the existing plain-`<section>` idiom already used throughout this file (e.g. the \"Top fee payers\" section at lines 401-451) \u2014 not `SectionAnchor` (that's used elsewhere in the app, e.g. `incident-timeline.tsx`, but this file's own convention is the plain bordered `<section>`). Populate it with: a small stat row (network `distinct_removers`, `removals`, `removals_per_remover`) using the same inline pattern as the fee-payers header count (line 406-408), then a per-subnet leaderboard table reusing the exact `TH`-styled `<table>` idiom from \"Top fee payers\" (lines 410-445) with columns Subnet / Removals / Distinct removers / Removals per remover, each subnet row linking to `/subnets/$netuid` (matching the `Link` pattern already used for `/accounts/$ss58` at line 424-431). Handle the empty leaderboard the same way as the existing empty states in this file (e.g. line 447-449's `<p className=\"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-muted\">`).\n- Coordination note: this issue is explicitly \"next to the network operations leaderboard\" from **#3463** (`GET /api/v1/chain/serving` + `/chain/prometheus`, also confirmed to have zero UI touchpoint \u2014 no `chainServingQuery`/`chainPrometheusQuery` exists either). Both issues land new sections in the same `ExplorerDashboard()` function in `explorer.tsx` \u2014 coordinate placement (this \"churn\" panel should sit directly beside or below #3463's operations leaderboard) and expect a merge conflict if both PRs are in flight simultaneously; whichever lands second should rebase onto the first rather than duplicating layout scaffolding.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Diff touches at least one file under `apps/ui/src/routes/` (specifically `explorer.tsx`), not just `queries.ts`/`types.ts`\n- [ ] `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` gains a `chainAxonRemovalsQuery` function and `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` gains a `ChainAxonRemovals` type\n- [ ] `ExplorerDashboard()` in `explorer.tsx` calls `chainAxonRemovalsQuery(win)` via `useSuspenseQuery`, consistent with the four sibling chain queries already called there\n- [ ] The rendered panel shows the network rollup (distinct removers, total removals, removals-per-remover) and a per-subnet leaderboard table with working `/subnets/$netuid` links, respecting the shared `7d`/`30d` window toggle\n- [ ] `/api/v1/chain/axon-removals` is added to the `ApiSourceFooter` `paths` array in `explorer.tsx`\n- [ ] Loading + empty + error states handled, matching the existing convention in `explorer.tsx` (page-level `Suspense`/`QueryErrorBoundary` for loading/error; a muted `<p>` fallback for an empty leaderboard, matching lines 447-449)\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Wiring the subnet-scoped `/api/v1/subnets/{netuid}/axon-removals` route or its existing `subnetAxonRemovalsQuery` \u2014 that's #3482 (subnet operational panel), a separate file (subnet detail page, not `explorer.tsx`)\n- Building #3463's operations leaderboard (serving/prometheus) \u2014 track that work in #3463 itself, even though both sections land in the same `ExplorerDashboard()` function\n- CSV export wiring for this leaderboard (the backend supports `?format=csv` but no CSV-download-button issue is scoped here; see the separate CSV-button issues #3402-3409 if one is later filed for the explorer page)\n\n## Size\n\nSize: XS \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
